pages.content:
### Countdown Loops & Boundary Invariants

In countdown loops, pay special attention to whether `0` should be included:

```java
// Case A: Excludes 0 (stops at 1)
int a = 3;
while (a > 0) {
    System.out.print(a + " "); // Prints: 3 2 1
    a--;
}

// Case B: Includes 0 (stops at 0)
int b = 3;
while (b >= 0) {
    System.out.print(b + " "); // Prints: 3 2 1 0
    b--;
}
```

Choosing between `>` and `>=` determines whether the base value 0 is executed.

