### Step Decrements and Non-Zero Termination

When decrementing by more than 1, the counter may overshoot zero into negative numbers:

```java
int i = 10;
while (i > 0) {
    System.out.print(i + " "); // Prints: 10 7 4 1
    i -= 3;
}
System.out.println("\nFinal i: " + i); // Final i is: -2!
```

Notice that the final value of `i` is `-2`, because `1 - 3 = -2`.

