pages.content:
### Early Termination with `break`

The `break` statement provides an immediate exit from a loop, typically when a search target or terminating condition is found:

```java
int i = 1;
while (i <= 10) {
    if (i == 5) {
        System.out.println("Target found at: " + i);
        break; // Exits loop immediately!
    }
    System.out.println(i);
    i++;
}
System.out.println("Post-loop code");
```

#### Key Points:
- Statements after `break` in the loop body are **not executed**.
- Execution jumps directly to the first statement outside the loop block.

