pages.content:
### The Input Validation Loop Pattern

Input validation loops prevent bad data from propagating through your application:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class InputValidation {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter a positive number: ");
        int num = scanner.nextInt();

        // Loop while input is INVALID
        while (num <= 0) {
            System.out.print("Invalid! Number must be > 0. Try again: ");
            num = scanner.nextInt();
        }

        System.out.println("Accepted valid input: " + num);
        scanner.close();
    }
}
```

#### Key Pattern:
The loop condition checks for **invalidity** (`num <= 0`). As long as the input is invalid, the loop continues prompting.

