pages.content:
### Sentinel and Flag-Controlled Loops

When a loop depends on a complex condition or an external event, a boolean flag provides clean control flow:

```java
boolean isRunning = true;
int attempts = 0;

while (isRunning) {
    attempts++;
    if (checkServerHealth()) {
        System.out.println("Server healthy!");
        isRunning = false; // Flag signals loop to stop
    } else if (attempts >= 5) {
        System.out.println("Max attempts reached!");
        isRunning = false;
    }
}
```

#### Advantages of Boolean Flags:
- Clearly documents the exit reason.
- Avoids multiple complicated conditions in the loop header.
- Keeps termination logic clean without scattering multiple `break` statements.

