pages.content:
### Nested While Loops

A nested while loop is a while loop placed inside the body of another while loop:

```java
int row = 1;
while (row <= 3) {
    int col = 1; // CRITICAL: Reset inner loop counter here!
    while (col <= 2) {
        System.out.print("(" + row + "," + col + ") ");
        col++;
    }
    System.out.println();
    row++;
}
```

#### Output:
```
(1,1) (1,2) 
(2,1) (2,2) 
(3,1) (3,2) 
```

#### The Reset Bug:
Notice that `int col = 1;` is initialized **inside** the outer loop. If it were declared outside the outer loop, it would not reset, and the inner loop would only execute on the very first row!

