pages.content:
### Two-Pointer Palindrome Verification

A while loop is the standard construct for palindrome verification using two converging pointers:

```java
public class PalindromeCheck {
    public static boolean isPalindrome(String str) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = str.length() - 1;

        while (left < right) {
            if (str.charAt(left) != str.charAt(right)) {
                return false; // Mismatch found
            }
            left++;
            right--;
        }
        return true; // All matched
    }
}
```

#### Why This Is Efficient:
- Compares characters from both ends inward.
- Runs in $O(N)$ time with $O(1)$ extra space.
- Terminates immediately on the first mismatched character.

