pages.content:
By default, loop counters increment by `1` using `i++`. In Java, you can use any valid assignment or arithmetic expression in the update clause to step by custom amounts.

### Stepping by Custom Increments

```java
public class StepRange {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Step by 2: Even numbers from 2 to 10
        System.out.print("Even numbers: ");
        for (int i = 2; i <= 10; i += 2) {
            System.out.print(i + " ");
        }
        System.out.println();

        // Step by 5: Multiples of 5 from 5 to 30
        System.out.print("Step of 5: ");
        for (int i = 5; i <= 30; i += 5) {
            System.out.print(i + " ");
        }
        System.out.println();

        // Multiplicative Step: Powers of 2
        System.out.print("Powers of 2: ");
        for (int i = 1; i <= 64; i *= 2) {
            System.out.print(i + " ");
        }
        System.out.println();
    }
}
```

**Output:**
```default
Even numbers: 2 4 6 8 10 
Step of 5: 5 10 15 20 25 30 
Powers of 2: 1 2 4 8 16 32 64 
```

> [!TIP]
> The update expression `i += step` is shorthand for `i = i + step`. Any valid reassignment expression can be placed in the third section of the `for` header.

